= Negotiations for a New Cabinet

With the dissolution of the United States of Indonesia and the reinauguration of the unitary state, the incumbent Hatta cabinet has resigned to make way for a new cabinet for the renascent Republic.

President Sukarno has conducted hearings with the representatives of most of the parties, consulting them on the matter of the composition and the program of the upcoming cabinet to be formed and in particular on the matter who shall be named to form the new cabinet.

- @natsir_pm: The President has appointed Mohammad Natsir..

@natsir_pm
subtitle: {!<div style="display: flex;justify-content: left;">
<img src="img/portraits/natsir.jpg" style="width: 100px;border: 5px solid var(--card-border-color);margin: 10px"> 
<div style="width: 300px;">Chairman of the executive council of the <span style="color: #000000;">**Masjumi**</span>, the party with the largest representation within the parliament.</div>
</div>!}
face-image: img/portraits/natsir.jpg

With Natsir's appointment, the politics of cabinet formation have gone into high gear. The main problems Natsir encountered are the relations between the <span style="color: #000000;">**Masjumi**</span> and the <span style="color: #900000;">**PNI**</span>, the second party with the largest parliamentary representation. Natsir believed that, as the party of the *formatuer* and intended prime minister, the <span style="color: #000000;">**Masjumi**</span> should have the largest leverage in forming the new cabinet. Moreover, the <span style="color: #000000;">**Masjumi**</span> and its various factions and member organisations are pressing him to make high demands. 

Natsir insists that the <span style="color: #000000;">**Masjumi**</span> should hold six positions in the cabinet: the prime ministership, three of the major portfolios, the Interior, Finance, and Defense, and the lesser Education and Religious Affairs portfolios. In turn, the <span style="color: #900000;">**PNI**</span> would gain the portfolios of Foreign Affairs, Information, Public Works, and Labor. Most of the party, however, believes that this arrangement is unfair and that the <span style="color: #900000;">**PNI**</span>, as the second largest party, should have greater influence within the cabinet. 

- @natsir_ye: Accept and join the cabinet.
- @natsir_no: These demands are outrageous!

@natsir_no

We have rejected Natsir's unfair offer, thus the <span style="color: #900000;">**PNI**</span> would not participate in his cabinet. It is likely that Natsir would return his mandate back to the President.

@natsir_ye
subtitle: Most of the party would be incensed.
on-arrival: sidik_dissent += 20; partindo_dissent += 20; sidik_strength -= 5; 
on-departure: first_cabinet_formed = 1; foreign_minister = 'Moekarto Notowidigdo'; foreign_minister_party = 'PNI'; enlightenment_minister = 'Arnold Mononutu'; enlightenment_minister_party = 'PNI'; publicworks_minister = 'Umar Bratakusumah'; publicworks_minister_party = 'PNI'; labor_minister = 'Wilopo'; labor_minister_party = 'PNI';

At last the first cabinet of the reborn republic is formulated, though at the cost of indignations and uproar within the <span style="color: #900000;">**PNI**</span>. Natsir reported back to the president that he had successfully formed a new cabinet.

As per the agreement, we are granted the portfolios of Foreign Affairs, Information, Public Works, and Labor. 

- @root: The cabinet is formed.

